helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04090200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150028	96			0	nb	You can include user data when you define conditions. To change your user data, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - User data\</emph\>. User data must be entered in the form of strings. You can query the user data with "==" (EQ), "!=" (NEQ), or "!"(NOT).				20130618 17:22:18
