helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\06100000.xhp	0	help	par_idN10895				0	nb	For Asian languages, select \<emph\>Match case \</emph\>to apply multi-level collation. In the multi-level collation, the primitive forms of the entries are first compared with the cases of the forms and diacritics ignored. If the forms are the same, the diacritics of the forms are compared. If the forms are still the same, the cases, character widths, and Japanese Kana differences of the forms are compared.				20130618 17:22:18
