helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154909	2			0	nb	Writes a record to a relative file or a sequence of bytes to a binary file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281	3			0	nb	See also: \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03020201.xhp\" name=\"Get\"\>\<item type=\"literal\"\>Get\</item\>\</link\> statement				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863	4			0	nb	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	5			0	nb	Put [#] FileNumber As Integer, [position], Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153190	6			0	nb	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120	7			0	nb	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression that defines the file that you want to write to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155411	8			0	nb	\<emph\>Position: \</emph\>For relative files (random access files), the number of the record that you want to write.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576	9			0	nb	For binary files (binary access), the position of the byte in the file where you want to start writing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729	10			0	nb	\<emph\>Variable:\</emph\> Name of the variable that you want to write to the file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	11			0	nb	Note for relative files: If the contents of this variable does not match the length of the record that is specified in the \<emph\>Len\</emph\> clause of the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> statement, the space between the end of the newly written record and the next record is padded with existing data from the file that you are writing to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020204.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	12			0	nb	Note for binary files: The contents of the variables are written to the specified position, and the file pointer is inserted directly after the last byte. No space is left between the records.				20130618 17:22:18
