helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142	6			0	nb	DIM sPar3 AS STRING				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576	7			0	nb	Dim declares local variables within subroutines. Global variables are declared with the PUBLIC or the PRIVATE statement.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	8			0	nb	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149412	9			0	nb	[ReDim]Dim VarName [(start To end)] [As VarType][, VarName2 [(start To end)] [As VarType][,...]]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147397	10			0	nb	Parameters:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730	11			0	nb	\<emph\>VarName:\</emph\> Any variable or array name.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125	12			0	nb	\<emph\>Start, End:\</emph\> Numerical values or constants that define the number of elements (NumberElements=(end-start)+1) and the index range.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153877	13			0	nb	Start and End can be numerical expressions if ReDim is applied at the procedure level.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03102100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153510	14			0	nb	\<emph\>VarType:\</emph\> Key word that declares the data type of a variable.				20130618 17:22:18
