helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149346	52			0	nb	Creates a Listener instance.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153681	51			0	nb	Many Uno interfaces let you register listeners on a special listener interface. This allows you to listen for specific events and call up the appropriate listener method. The CreateUnoListener function waits for the called listener interface and then passes the interface an object that the interface supports. This object is then passed to the method to register the listener.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148685	50			0	nb	Syntax:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143228	49			0	nb	oListener = CreateUnoListener( Prefixname, ListenerInterfaceName )				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574	48			0	nb	Example:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046	47			0	nb	The following example is based on a Basic library object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136	46			0	nb	Dim oListener				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148944	45			0	nb	oListener = CreateUnoListener( "ContListener_","com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener" )				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149294	44			0	nb	The CreateUnoListener method requires two parameters. The first is a prefix and is explained in detail below. The second parameter is the fully qualified name of the Listener interface that you want to use.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	43			0	nb	The Listener must then be added to the Broadcaster Object. This is done by calling the appropriate method for adding a Listener. These methods always follow the pattern "addFooListener", where "Foo" is the Listener Interface Type, without the 'X'. In this example, the addContainerListener method is called to register the XContainerListener:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154164	42			0	nb	Dim oLib				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154940	41			0	nb	oLib = BasicLibraries.Library1 ' Library1 must exist!				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150359	40			0	nb	oLib.addContainerListener( oListener ) ' Register the listener				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138	39			0	nb	The Listener is now registered. When an event occurs, the corresponding Listener calls the appropriate method from the com.sun.star.container.XContainerListener Interface.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148922	38			0	nb	The prefix calls registered Listeners from Basic-subroutines. The Basic run-time system searches for Basic-subroutines or functions that have the name "PrefixListenerMethode" and calls them when found. Otherwise, a run-time error occurs.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03132000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150768	37			0	nb	In this example, the Listener-Interface uses the following methods:				20130618 17:22:18
