helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600	34			0	nb	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969	35			0	nb	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640	36			0	nb	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	nb	Forene data				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\consolidate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	nb	\<bookmark_value\>consolidating data\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ranges; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>combining;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; combining\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>data; merging cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;data ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
