helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445	17			0	nb	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565	18			0	nb	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255	19			0	nb	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
