helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417	90			0	nb	Nominal interest refers to the amount of interest due at the end of a calculation period. Effective interest increases with the number of payments made. In other words, interest is often paid in installments (for example, monthly or quarterly) before the end of the calculation period.				20130618 17:22:18
