helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467	336			0	nb	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000	337			0	nb	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020	559			0	nb	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792	629			0	nb	Hvis begge parametrene Tall og Trinn er negative og verdien Modus er lik null eller ikke angitt, vil resultatene i $[officename] og Excel avvike etter importering. Hvis du eksporterer regnearket til Excel, kan du bruke Modus=1 for å se de samme resultatene i Excel og i Calc.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697	338			0	nb	Eksempel				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710	339			0	nb	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				20130618 17:22:18
