helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3154304	80			0	nb	            \<emph\>X\</emph\> is the number of successes in a set of trials.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3147492	81			0	nb	            \<emph\>Trials\</emph\> is the number of independent trials.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3146085	82			0	nb	            \<emph\>SP\</emph\> is the probability of success on each trial.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3149760	83			0	nb	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calculates the probability of a single event and \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calculates the cumulative probability.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151171	84			0	nb	Eksempel				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3145666	85			0	nb	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;0)\</item\> shows (if the values \<item type=\"input\"\>0\</item\> to \<item type=\"input\"\>12\</item\> are entered in A1) the probabilities for 12 flips of a coin that \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> will come up exactly the number of times entered in A1.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	par_id3150120	86			0	nb	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=BINOMDIST(A1;12;0.5;1)\</item\> shows the cumulative probabilities for the same series. For example, if A1 = \<item type=\"input\"\>4\</item\>, the cumulative probability of the series is 0, 1, 2, 3 or 4 times \<emph\>Heads\</emph\> (non-exclusive OR).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060181.xhp	0	help	bm_id0119200902432928				0	nb	\<bookmark_value\>CHISQINV function\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
